abstract: >-
  Difference-side arithmetic of the 3x3 magic square of squares problem:
  a seven-line normal form (three same-difference square progressions on a
  transversal frame); three explicit mechanisms producing infinite (8,7)
  near-miss families with a complete least-shift law; the interaction
  surface for the eighth line, its saturation and full S5 cone monodromy;
  imported fixed-difference finiteness with one completely closed fibre
  and a finite-Kummer-class stop; a five-term S-unit support law with an
  exact mod-8 endpoint/interior table and, for primitive positive
  configurations, the complete exclusion of the supports {2,3} and
  {2,3,p}; and the four-prime frontier stated exactly and left open. Every computation ships as an exact machine-checkable
  certificate replayed by a standard-library verifier; commercial-CAS
  evidence enters only as hash-verified frozen transcripts with their
  exact calculator inputs. Classical ingredients are attributed; no
  priority or firstness is claimed.
